# Arc Foundry — Debug and automation surface

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
Arc Foundry carries a debugging and automation surface, `window.__foundry`, so the yard
can be posed and read from code without moving a real pointer or waiting on real time.

You implement it. Every operation this file specifies is a deliverable, and the build
installs the finished surface on `window.__foundry` as soon as the game has initialized.
Every scenario driven from code reaches the game through it, so it is present and exactly
as specified here.

Each operation is a reading or a pose. A pose sets one thing and leaves the rest of the
game as it stands, so a caller that wants several things arranged makes several calls, in
the order it wants them, and nothing it does not ask for happens. A pose arranges the
yard through the same systems play uses: a placed rock rolls through the real press, a
harvested candidate becomes a component through the real harvest, a combine resolves
through the real combine, and a released unit walks the real pathfinder. A pose
establishes a precondition and never an outcome; what happens next comes from advancing
the real simulation.

The surface is inert during normal play, doing nothing until something calls it.
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
